{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 120,
    "dDurationMs": 5940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In my last video we performed an experiment\nin which two identical wood blocks were shot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6060,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the same rifle, one through the center\nof mass and the other one slightly off to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9990,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one side."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10990,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you haven’t seen that video yet,\nthen click here now and go and watch it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14420,
    "dDurationMs": 6300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or, if you are on a mobile device, click the\nlink in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20720,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the question was: Compared to the block\nshot straight through its center, how high"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24780,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would the block shot to one side go?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27190,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now 60 percent of you predicted that it wouldn’t\ngo as high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31480,
    "dDurationMs": 3489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e It didn’t seem as high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34969,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Now check out the high speed footage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37309,
    "dDurationMs": 1981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Oh, no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39290,
    "dDurationMs": 1639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e You can clearly see that both blocks..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40929,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e What?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41929,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e ... go to the exact same height."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43139,
    "dDurationMs": 1051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Oh, come on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44190,
    "dDurationMs": 2649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Nineteen percent said that it would go\nhigher."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46839,
    "dDurationMs": 5730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And only 21 percent correctly predicted that\nboth blocks would go to the exact same height."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52569,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So most of us got it wrong the first time\naround and that includes Henry and me and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56859,
    "dDurationMs": 2170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Destin who has a lot of experience with this\nstuff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59029,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e I mean, I can’t tell you how many times\nI have hit wood with a rifle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62639,
    "dDurationMs": 3861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e So even experienced and intelligent people\nget it wrong sometimes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66500,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case I think the result was particularly\ncounter intuitive, because the spinning block"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70640,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clearly ended up with more energy than the\nother block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73890,
    "dDurationMs": 3670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I asked you guys to make me a video response\nand explain what is happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77560,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is what I received."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79400,
    "dDurationMs": 9830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e If you imagine the bullet traveling through\nthe center of the block, then..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89230,
    "dDurationMs": 6520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "[multiple voices]"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95750,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Whoa."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99000,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is a lot of video responses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100740,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that is not even all of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102250,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have got to say I was blown away by all\nof the great video responses I received."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107430,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You guys are awesome and really, really appreciate\nall the effort you went to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111850,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, some of you actually replicated\nthe experiment, perhaps with different setups."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117590,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Oh, ah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119630,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e The experiment was featured on blog posts,\nincluding Scientific America and Wired."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124090,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is an interactive simulation you can\ntry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126530,
    "dDurationMs": 1220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Link is in the description."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127750,
    "dDurationMs": 1979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And someone even made a web comic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129729,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is so incredible, you know, watching all\nof those video responses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133239,
    "dDurationMs": 1711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I did watch all of them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134950,
    "dDurationMs": 5619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That was my proudest moment making this YouTube\nchannel, seeing all of you guys doing science"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140569,
    "dDurationMs": 2771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and getting so involved and putting in so\nmuch effort."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143340,
    "dDurationMs": 1220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It just blows my mind."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144560,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is amazing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145560,
    "dDurationMs": 1690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you guys so much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147250,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you, thank you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148250,
    "dDurationMs": 3409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can’t even put it into words how awesome\nit is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151659,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whoo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153019,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what is the answer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154629,
    "dDurationMs": 4401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How could two identical blocks shot with the\nsame rifle end up with different amounts of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159030,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160030,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, some of you felt that the amount of\nrotational energy would be basically insignificant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164390,
    "dDurationMs": 6790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e What if the amount of energy necessary\nto get that very small block rotating really"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171180,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is negligible in comparison to the amount\nof energy necessary to lift it into the air"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177140,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and resist gravity?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178140,
    "dDurationMs": 4769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Well, we can calculate it, because the\nspinning block was rotating at about 11 times"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182909,
    "dDurationMs": 1031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183940,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can calculate that its rotational energy\nwould be equal to 50 percent of the gravitational"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189330,
    "dDurationMs": 2879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "potential energy when those blocks were at\ntheir peak."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192209,
    "dDurationMs": 5441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the spinning block actually had 1.5 times\nthe energy of the non-rotating block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197650,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in my books that is not negligible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200090,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what else could be causing this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202370,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, some of you actually measured the height\ndifference using pixel counters and found"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206750,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the blocks didn't go to exactly the same\nheight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210230,
    "dDurationMs": 3569,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this raises an important question, which\nis: How different would those heights have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213799,
    "dDurationMs": 3731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be before you can think that there really\nis a difference there?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217530,
    "dDurationMs": 4269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, given that the rotational energy is\nabout 50 percent of the gravitational potential"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221799,
    "dDurationMs": 3381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy, you might expect the spinning block\nto go half as high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225180,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But looking at the video footage you can clearly\nsee it doesn’t go half as high."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228950,
    "dDurationMs": 2659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It goes basically to the same height."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231609,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To know for sure, you would probably want\nto do the experiment a number of times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235309,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In science you have got to repeat things and\nmake sure what you saw is not just a fluke,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238969,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it will happen every time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240809,
    "dDurationMs": 4591,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in fact, we did repeat the experiment\na number of times and here are all of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245400,
    "dDurationMs": 9239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blocks lined up side by side so you can compare\ntheir heights."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254639,
    "dDurationMs": 3141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The blocks clearly do not all go to the same\nheight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257780,
    "dDurationMs": 2479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might say: Derek, you were tricking\nus."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260259,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You just picked the two that went the closest\nand used those."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262699,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263699,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I did do that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264699,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the point is do the spinning blocks go\nsystematically to a lower height than the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268849,
    "dDurationMs": 1070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "non-spinning blocks?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269919,
    "dDurationMs": 3941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I think from the video footage the answer\nis clearly no."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273860,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why not?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275560,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, another common response I saw was that\nair resistance must play a role, that the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280840,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spinning block exposes a small surface area\nas it is traveling upwards and this means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286030,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is less air resistance impeding it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288050,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even with a lower velocity it could make\nit to the same height as the non-spinning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292830,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293830,
    "dDurationMs": 3429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you can do the calculation and find that\nthe difference in air resistance would be,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297259,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at most, about 0.6 percent of the weight of\nthe block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301169,
    "dDurationMs": 2391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, negligible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303560,
    "dDurationMs": 2579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what is the real answer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306139,
    "dDurationMs": 4391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, there are a number of ways of approaching\nthe problem and I saw you guys try almost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310530,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of them: force, torque, momentum, energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314500,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the easiest one of these is the law of\nconservation of momentum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318120,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You see, when the bullet is fired out of the\nrifle it has a certain amount of momentum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322470,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entirely in the vertical direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324970,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when the bullet becomes lodged in the\nblock the bullet and block together must have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329520,
    "dDurationMs": 2489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that same momentum that the bullet had."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332009,
    "dDurationMs": 4401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now it doesn’t matter where on the block\nthe bullet hits, because the bullet had a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336410,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "certain momentum before it hit the block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338240,
    "dDurationMs": 4299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The block and bullet together afterwards must\nhave that amount of momentum upwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342539,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this means regardless of whether the block\nis spinning or not, it must have the same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346699,
    "dDurationMs": 5421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "upwards velocity, so that it has the same\nmomentum, so it will got the same height regardless"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352120,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of whether it is spinning or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354039,
    "dDurationMs": 2761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is simple conservation of momentum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356800,
    "dDurationMs": 2139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Momentum is always, always conserved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358939,
    "dDurationMs": 2271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is something you can always rely on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361210,
    "dDurationMs": 2079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it is why you should think about it first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363289,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But some of you may say: Ok, well, there is\nalso angular momentum in the spinning block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367569,
    "dDurationMs": 4671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the point is: Angular moment and linear\nmomentum are independent and they are conserved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372240,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "independently."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373240,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can simply think about the upward momentum\nof the bullet and that is going to have to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377300,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be the upward momentum of those two blocks\nand it doesn’t matter that one is spinning,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381139,
    "dDurationMs": 3191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they have the same total linear momentum\nupwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384330,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they have to go to the same height."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386410,
    "dDurationMs": 5259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if that is the case, why does the spinning\nblock end up with this extra rotational energy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391669,
    "dDurationMs": 3881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the thing about energy is it is a little\nbit tricky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395550,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although total energy is conserved, the energy\nof motion—which is called kinetic energy—is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400580,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not conserved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401990,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what happens is as the bullet strikes the\nwood a lot of its kinetic energy is lost,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407490,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heating up the wood, creating sound and deforming\nthat wood block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411560,
    "dDurationMs": 4109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it would be possible for the rotating block\nto end up with more energy of motion, more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415669,
    "dDurationMs": 6701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kinetic energy, if the bullet loses less energy\ndeforming the wood and heating it up and creating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422370,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that sound."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423870,
    "dDurationMs": 4310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this kind of makes a little bit of intuitive\nsense, because if you imagine the bullet entering"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428180,
    "dDurationMs": 5859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the block on the side, the block will be moving\naway from it faster, because it is rotating."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434039,
    "dDurationMs": 3832,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that may mean that the bullet doesn’t\npenetrate in as far and so it wouldn’t lose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437871,
    "dDurationMs": 4709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as much energy as it is entering the wood,\nwhich explains why the block has extra energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442580,
    "dDurationMs": 3329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "allowing it to rotate and go the same height\nas the other block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445909,
    "dDurationMs": 3951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s have a look at how far in the bullet\nwent into each block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449860,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is our first test."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450860,
    "dDurationMs": 1299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here we go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452159,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the one where it went straight in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453479,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e There."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455409,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457339,
    "dDurationMs": 2471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e And we come over here to the opposite end."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459810,
    "dDurationMs": 1729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e This is where the bullet went in off center."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461539,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e It is not going in here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463389,
    "dDurationMs": 1411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See where my...?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464800,
    "dDurationMs": 2739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Yeah, let’s see the other one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467539,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Ok."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469069,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is all the way in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472349,
    "dDurationMs": 1861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is part way in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474210,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e So the bullet didn’t go as far into the\nspinning block."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478620,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e Right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479720,
    "dDurationMs": 1479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\u003e\u003e So that was pretty convincing evidence."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481199,
    "dDurationMs": 4071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But just to be extra sure we x-rayed both\nblocks and this is what we saw."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 485270,
    "dDurationMs": 5369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am going to overlay the blocks so we can\nsee the difference in penetration depth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490639,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hang on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491639,
    "dDurationMs": 5791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It looks like both blocks penetrated each\nblock to the same depth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497430,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So does that mean our theory is wrong?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499550,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, let’s think about how different the\nbullet depths should be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503120,
    "dDurationMs": 4819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, when the bullet strikes the block\nit actually loses 97 percent of its original"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507939,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "kinetic energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508939,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the amount of rotational energy the spinning\nblock has only works out to about one percent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513889,
    "dDurationMs": 2351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the original kinetic energy of the bullet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516240,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we would only expect a difference in depths\nof about one percent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520740,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for our measurements, that would be about\na tenth of a millimeter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524670,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That would be immeasurable and that is what\nwe see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529430,
    "dDurationMs": 5630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So although this answer is a little bit unsatisfying,\nat least it is the truth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535060,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As an extra challenge, I want you guys to\nthink about how we could perhaps modify this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539060,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experiment so the difference in bullet depth\nwould be measurable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542490,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can leave your answers in the comments\nor make me another video response, because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545660,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I love those so much."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550570,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode of Veritasium was brought to\nyou by Audible.com, a leading provider of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554690,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "audio books with over 100,000 titles in all\ndifferent types of literature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now today I wanted to recommend a book that\nchanged my life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561080,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is called The Four Hour Work Week and it\nis by Tim Faris who I actually got to meet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565010,
    "dDurationMs": 1579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this year at VidCon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566589,
    "dDurationMs": 2891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I read this book about three years ago\nwhen I was thinking about quitting my job"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569480,
    "dDurationMs": 1229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and starting this YouTube channel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570709,
    "dDurationMs": 2551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it is one of the things that contributed\nto my decision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573260,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you are thinking about quitting your\njob, perhaps this is the book for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576910,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can actually download it for free by going\nto Audible.com/Veritasium, click the link"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581150,
    "dDurationMs": 4239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the description or you can choose any other\nbook of your choosing for a one month free"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585389,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586389,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So thanks to Audible for supporting Veritasium\nand thanks to you for watching."
    } ]
  } ]
}
